<newsitem itemid="121803" id="root" date="1996-10-16" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Smiths Industries year profit rises.</title>
<headline>Smiths Industries year profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to August 3</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		36.6		   vs 30.7</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 16.2		   vs 14.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     165		    vs 138</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,008		  vs 899</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 159.0 to 165.0 million stg. Dividend forecasts ranged from 15.7p to 16.0p.</p>
<p>Above share and pretax profit figures exclude exceptionals.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 168.1		  vs 140.9</p>
<p> Exceptional gain	 5.0		    vs 0.5 loss</p>
<p> Net interest	     2.7		    vs 2.4</p>
<p> Tax			  52.6		   vs 44.1</p>
<p> Net taxed		  117.8		  vs 93.9</p>
<p> Final dividend (pence) 10.6		   vs 9.35</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan. 1</p>
<p> Div registration date  Nov. 5</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Oct. 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptional items in the current year included a cash distribution of about 14.2 million stg after costs related to the disposal of housing estates owned by an unconsolidated unit and a 9.1 million stg charge for unrealised profit in stock related to the company's increased equity in Japan Medico Ltd.</p>
<p>Year-ago exceptional items included a 3.0 million stg profit on property sales and a 3.5 million stg loss on sale of businesses.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
